! Tetragonal cobalt, converged self-consistently WITH spin-orbit coupling: the
! relaxed magnetocrystalline anisotropy.
!
! Deliberately the same cell, dataset, cutoffs and k-grid as
! co-tetragonal-anisotropy-soc.in, which is the force theorem's one-shot leg,
! so the two routes to the same quantity can be differenced on this cell and
! the difference is the relaxation energy rather than a change of setup.
!
! Three things the relaxed route needs and the theorem does not:
!
!   * calculation = 'scf'. There is no handoff and no second leg -- each
!     direction is one ordinary self-consistent run with the fully-relativistic
!     dataset, and the anisotropy is a difference of TOTAL energies.
!   * conv_thr at 1e-10. A uniaxial cobalt anisotropy is a few tenths of a meV,
!     which is ~1e-5 Ry on totals of order 100 Ry, so the threshold has to sit
!     several orders below the answer. The force theorem never needs this
!     because every term but the band sum cancels between two directions by
!     construction; here nothing cancels and the subtraction is done on the
!     printed numbers.
!   * nosym. A noncollinear magnetic run reduces its k-grid with the MAGNETIC
!     symmetry group, which depends on where the moment points -- so two
!     directions would otherwise be sampled on two different wedges. For a
!     total energy that is worse than for a band sum: the Ewald and Hartree
!     terms come along too, so the contamination is not confined to the bands.
!
! The direction is set by the workflow through angle1/angle2, not here, so the
! values below are the starting point of the first direction only.
&control
   calculation = 'scf'
/
&system
   ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 4.60, celldm(3) = 1.30, nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
   noncolin = .true., lspinorb = .true., nosym = .true.,
   ecutwfc = 20.0, ecutrho = 160.0,
   occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'mv', degauss = 0.02,
   starting_magnetization(1) = 0.6,
   angle1(1) = 0.0, angle2(1) = 0.0,
/
&electrons
   conv_thr = 1.0e-10
   mixing_beta = 0.3
/
ATOMIC_SPECIES
Co 58.933 Co.rel-pbe-nd-rrkjus.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
Co 0.0 0.0 0.0
K_POINTS automatic
3 3 2 0 0 0
